Comment to 1446.
----------
A useful way to check for the correct installation of the serial link 
is shown below.  I use it in my terminal program "PocPac", and also 
find it useful to check for the presence of any directory on my 3a.

There is a bug in some of the earlier 3a's, which prevented serial 
comms from working after you tried to open TTY:A without the RS232 
lead connected.  Luckily there is a patch for this, but it's 
worthwhile for programmers to incorporate some code like this to 
prevent a lot of grief to those unaware of it.
        
                
IF ckpth%:("LOC::C:\")
        ALERT("Serial Lead Not Plugged In !!","Abort")
        STOP
ENDIF

PROC ckpth%:(cpth$)
        LOCAL h%,p$(128)
        p$=cpth$+"*.*"
        IF IOOPEN(h%,p$,$30)
                RETURN -1
        ELSE
                IOCLOSE(h%) :RETURN 0
        ENDIF
ENDP

Roger


